00:12:20,400 --> 00:12:21,400
What is she saying?

249
00:12:21,400 --> 00:12:22,400
So it's got a different meaning.

250
00:12:22,920 --> 00:12:23,080
All right.

251
00:12:23,400 --> 00:12:24,980
So she's basically saying this should work.

252
00:12:25,240 --> 00:12:26,440
This should fix your problem.

253
00:12:27,200 --> 00:12:28,680
So that should do the trick.

254
00:12:29,280 --> 00:12:37,030
So Marco, I've been having this itch on my foot and I just can't seem to figure out what to do with it.

255
00:12:37,480 --> 00:12:37,930
Do you have any suggestions?

256
00:12:38,550 --> 00:12:38,730
Yeah.

257
00:12:38,850 --> 00:12:41,890
You should maybe just put some ointment on it and that should do the trick.

258
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:42,530
All right.

259
00:12:43,240 --> 00:12:44,240
Cool.

260
00:12:44,240 --> 00:12:45,240
Thanks for the suggestion.

261
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:46,240
Yeah.

262
00:12:46,240 --> 00:12:47,240
So very easy.

263
00:12:47,240 --> 00:12:48,240
It's just a way of saying that should solve your problem.

264
00:12:48,240 --> 00:12:49,240
All right.

265
00:12:49,240 --> 00:12:50,240
Great.

266
00:12:50,240 --> 00:12:53,520
So that's the trick or it will do the trick.

267
00:12:53,520 --> 00:12:55,790
And well, we have one last phrase, all set.

268
00:12:56,800 --> 00:12:57,190
All set.

269
00:12:57,800 --> 00:13:04,250
So this is another phrase that has two words that always go together to mean, well, we're finished.

270
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:05,110
We're done.

271
00:13:06,040 --> 00:13:06,420
Everything is ready.

272
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:07,380
Everything is ready.

273
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:08,980
We're all set to go on vacation.

274
00:13:09,440 --> 00:13:10,260
So my bags are packed.

275
00:13:10,440 --> 00:13:11,520
I have my passports.

276
00:13:11,520 --> 00:13:12,140
We are all set.

277
00:13:12,800 --> 00:13:14,860
Or after a meeting, you can say, are we all set here?

278
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:16,480
That means, are we finished?

279
00:13:16,480 --> 00:13:17,140
Is it time to leave?

280
00:13:17,840 --> 00:13:17,980
Very good.

281
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:20,100
So we are almost all set.

282
00:13:20,520 --> 00:13:22,520
Let's listen to this dialogue one last time.

283
00:13:29,370 --> 00:13:29,810
Okay.

284
00:13:30,680 --> 00:13:32,530
Let's go through this one more time.

285
00:13:33,320 --> 00:13:36,010
I don't want any more ruined or dyed blouses.

286
00:13:36,550 --> 00:13:36,970
I know.

287
00:13:37,070 --> 00:13:37,270
I know.

288
00:13:38,520 --> 00:13:39,520
Okay.

289
00:13:39,520 --> 00:13:45,630
So I had to separate the colors from the whites and put them in this strange looking contraption so-called washing machine.

290
00:13:46,120 --> 00:13:46,350
Right.

291
00:13:46,790 --> 00:13:50,290
You have to turn it on and program it depending on what type of clothes you're washing.

292
00:13:50,690 --> 00:13:53,970
For example, for delicates, you should set a shorter washing cycle.

293
00:13:54,510 --> 00:13:57,450
Also, be sure to use fabric softener and this detergent when washing.

294
00:13:57,930 --> 00:13:58,870
So complicated.

295
00:13:59,730 --> 00:14:00,130
Okay.

296
00:14:00,290 --> 00:14:01,790
What about this red wine stain?

297
00:14:02,290 --> 00:14:03,290
How do I get it out?

298
00:14:03,690 --> 00:14:08,530
Since this is a white T-shirt, you can just pour a little bit of bleach on it and it will do the trick.

299
00:14:08,950 --> 00:14:09,270
Cool.

300
00:14:09,770 --> 00:14:12,870
Then I can just throw everything in the dryer for an hour and it's all set, right?

301
00:14:13,250 --> 00:14:13,590
No.

302
00:14:14,880 --> 00:14:19,680
If you're washing delicates and cotton, you should set the dryer to medium heat and for 20 minutes.

303
00:14:19,950 --> 00:14:20,470
You know what?

304
00:14:21,230 --> 00:14:22,490
I'll just have everything dry cleaned.

305
00:14:30,400 --> 00:14:32,080
Have you ever had any laundry mishaps?

306
00:14:32,080 --> 00:14:35,720
Have you ever lost a sock, dyed something?

307
00:14:35,720 --> 00:14:36,380
Have I ever.

308
00:14:37,240 --> 00:14:38,740
I hate doing the laundry.

309
00:14:39,800 --> 00:14:40,800
Why?

310
00:14:40,800 --> 00:14:41,800
So much.

311
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:42,800
It's time consuming.

312
00:14:42,800 --> 00:14:46,600
It takes a lot of time and I just have no patience.

313
00:14:46,600 --> 00:14:55,040
And so normally, when I was in college, I would take all of my laundry in a bag and I'd throw it in the washing machine and I'd put it on cold.

314
00:14:55,040 --> 00:14:58,960
Because cold water, it's okay for all colors, but hot water makes the colors bleed.

315
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:08,010
I took out the clothes and put them in the dryer and afterwards I saw all my clothes were clean except for my three sweaters, which were small enough for babies.

316
00:15:08,550 --> 00:15:10,070
Oh, you shrunk it.

317
00:15:10,830 --> 00:15:13,550
I shrunk three brand new sweaters.

318
00:15:15,430 --> 00:15:20,310
The problem that I have when doing laundry is that I forget that I started doing laundry.

319
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:27,480
So all of a sudden, I'm doing laundry in the morning and then clothes are washed, but they're still in the washing machine.

320
00:15:27,480 --> 00:15:28,670
And I remember the next day.

321
00:15:29,280 --> 00:15:32,040
So then the clothes are smelling kind of humid.

322
00:15:32,480 --> 00:15:33,360
Because they're moldy.

323
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:37,000
So I have to rewash them and it's just a pain.

324
00:15:37,760 --> 00:15:41,920
And doing laundry is sometimes so time consuming, but let us know what you think.

325
00:15:41,920 --> 00:15:45,050
Do you like doing laundry or have you ever lost a sock?

326
00:15:45,280 --> 00:15:48,960
I think everyone has lost a sock or something in the washing, right?

327
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:49,960
I don't know what happens.

328
00:15:49,960 --> 00:15:52,320
I think there's a secret home for socks somewhere.

329
00:15:52,320 --> 00:15:53,480
It's so weird.

330
00:15:53,480 --> 00:15:54,830
Maybe it's in Australia or something.

